{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Namma Space — End-to-End 3D Reconstruction Training Pipeline\n",
    "### Techfest, IIT Bombay — Spatial Engine\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook trains a **3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS)** digital twin from a standard smartphone video.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Pipeline Flow:**\n",
    "1. GPU & CUDA Environment Setup\n",
    "2. COLMAP & Nerfstudio (`splatfacto`) Installation\n",
    "3. Input Video Ingestion (Upload or Google Drive)\n",
    "4. Automated Structure-from-Motion (COLMAP pose estimation & sparse reconstruction)\n",
    "5. 3D Gaussian Splatting Model Training (`splatfacto`)\n",
    "6. Web-Ready 3D Model Export (`.ply` / `.splat`)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1: Verify Hardware Accelerator\n",
    "Make sure **Runtime > Change runtime type > Hardware accelerator** is set to **T4 GPU** or **A100 GPU**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!nvidia-smi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2: Install System Dependencies (COLMAP, FFmpeg, Ninja)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install COLMAP and build tools\n",
    "!apt-get update -y && apt-get install -y colmap ffmpeg ninja-build"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3: Install Nerfstudio & Gaussian Splatting Engine\n",
    "Nerfstudio's `splatfacto` is the industry standard for fast, high-quality 3D Gaussian Splatting."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pip install --upgrade pip\n",
    "!pip install torch torchvision --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121\n",
    "!pip install nerfstudio"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4: Mount Google Drive or Upload Video Capture\n",
    "You can either mount Google Drive (recommended for large 4K smartphone videos) or upload directly."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "from google.colab import drive\n",
    "\n",
    "# Mount Drive (optional, uncomment if using Drive)\n",
    "# drive.mount('/content/drive')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Workspace directory setup\n",
    "WORKSPACE_DIR = \"/content/namma_space\"\n",
    "DATA_DIR = os.path.join(WORKSPACE_DIR, \"data\")\n",
    "OUTPUT_DIR = os.path.join(WORKSPACE_DIR, \"outputs\")\n",
    "EXPORT_DIR = os.path.join(WORKSPACE_DIR, \"exports\")\n",
    "\n",
    "os.makedirs(DATA_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "os.makedirs(OUTPUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "os.makedirs(EXPORT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Workspace initialized at {WORKSPACE_DIR}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 4b: Provide Your Smartphone Video\n",
    "Place your input video path below. \n",
    "- If uploaded to Colab directly: `INPUT_VIDEO = \"/content/room_capture.mp4\"`\n",
    "- Or upload using the Colab file upload widget below:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import files\n",
    "\n",
    "# If you haven't uploaded your video yet, run this cell to upload directly:\n",
    "uploaded = files.upload()\n",
    "video_filename = list(uploaded.keys())[0]\n",
    "INPUT_VIDEO = os.path.abspath(video_filename)\n",
    "print(f\"Using input video: {INPUT_VIDEO}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 5: End-to-End Structure-from-Motion (COLMAP via `ns-process-data`)\n",
    "This step:\n",
    "- Extracts optimal keyframes from your video (at 2-3 fps)\n",
    "- Runs feature matching via COLMAP\n",
    "- Reconstructs camera positions and sparse geometry"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "PROCESSED_DATA_DIR = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"processed_room\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Automatically run frame extraction and COLMAP feature matching\n",
    "!ns-process-data video \\\n",
    "    --data \"{INPUT_VIDEO}\" \\\n",
    "    --output-dir \"{PROCESSED_DATA_DIR}\" \\\n",
    "    --num-frames-target 250 \\\n",
    "    --matching-method exhaustive"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 6: Train the 3D Gaussian Splatting Model (`splatfacto`)\n",
    "This trains the 3D Gaussian representations in spatial coordinates with full photometric rendering."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Train splatfacto model (Gaussian Splatting)\n",
    "# 15,000 - 30,000 steps produces high-fidelity photorealistic indoor twins\n",
    "!ns-train splatfacto \\\n",
    "    --data \"{PROCESSED_DATA_DIR}\" \\\n",
    "    --output-dir \"{OUTPUT_DIR}\" \\\n",
    "    --max-num-iterations 20000 \\\n",
    "    --pipeline.model.cull-alpha-thresh 0.005 \\\n",
    "    --viewer.quit-on-train-completion True"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 7: Export Web-Ready 3D Digital Twin (`.ply` / `.splat`)\n",
    "Exports the trained Gaussian splats into a file ready to be loaded by Three.js in your Web Viewer."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import glob\n",
    "\n",
    "# Locate the generated config.yml from training\n",
    "config_files = glob.glob(f\"{OUTPUT_DIR}/**/config.yml\", recursive=True)\n",
    "if not config_files:\n",
    "    raise FileNotFoundError(\"Training configuration file not found!\")\n",
    "\n",
    "latest_config = max(config_files, key=os.path.getctime)\n",
    "print(f\"Found latest training config: {latest_config}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Export to standard Gaussian Splat PLY\n",
    "!ns-export gaussian-splat \\\n",
    "    --load-config \"{latest_config}\" \\\n",
    "    --output-dir \"{EXPORT_DIR}\"\n",
    "\n",
    "exported_plys = glob.glob(f\"{EXPORT_DIR}/*.ply\")\n",
    "print(f\"Successfully exported web model: {exported_plys}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 8: Download Exported 3D Model\n",
    "Download the generated `.ply` or `.splat` file to your laptop to place in your Web Viewer `public/` directory."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import files\n",
    "for ply in exported_plys:\n",
    "    files.download(ply)"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
